class:: Pn
summary:: repeatedly embed a pattern
related:: Classes/Pdup, Classes/Pseed
categories:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Repetition

description::
Repeat a pattern n times.

All Patterns implement the link::Classes/Pattern#-repeat:: method,
which is just another notation for code::Pn:::
In other words, code::Pn(pat, n):: is equivalent to code::pat.repeat(n)::.

For repetition strong::not:: of entire Patterns,
but of individual values (which in turn emphasis::can:: be patterns),
see link::Classes/Pdup:: and its equivalent link::Classes/Pattern#-dupEach::.


ClassMethods::

method::new

argument::pattern
the pattern to repeat

argument::repeats
Repeats the enclosed pattern strong::repeats:: times.

argument::key
If strong::key:: is non-nil, it sets the value of that key to true whenever it restarts the pattern.
This can be used to advance Patterns enclosed by link::Classes/Pgate::.

Examples::

code::
(
var a, b;
a = Pn(Pseq([1, 2, 3], 1), 4); // repeat pattern four times
b = a.asStream;
16.do({ b.next.postln });
)
::

Anchor::Examples::

code::
// When the pattern involves randomness,
// repetition of the Pattern does not entail repetition of output values:
(
var a, b;
a = Pn(Pwhite(1, 6, 3)), 4); // "repeat" the randomness four times
b = a.asStream;
16.do({ b.next.postln }); // oh well.
)

// to avoid this, use Pseed:
(
var a, b;
a = Pseed(Pn(1000, 4), Pwhite(1, 6, 3)); // repeat the randomness four times
b = a.asStream;
16.do({ b.next.postln }); // see?
)


// sound example
(
SynthDef(\help_sinegrain,
	{ |out = 0, freq = 440, sustain = 0.05|
		var env;
		env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.01, sustain, 0.2), doneAction: Done.freeSelf);
		Out.ar(out, SinOsc.ar(freq, 0, env))
	}).add;
)

(
var a;
a = Pn(Pshuf([1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3], 4)).asStream;
{
	loop {
		Synth(\help_sinegrain, [\freq, a.next * 600 + 300]);
		0.2.wait;
	}
}.fork;
)
::
